1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,748
Hello!

2
00:00:00,748 --> 00:00:06,497
This week you will write a Task 1 report of over one hundred and fifty words,

3
00:00:06,497 --> 00:00:08,961
and use three complex structures:

4
00:00:08,961 --> 00:00:12,396
relative clauses, conditionals, and inversion.

5
00:00:13,696 --> 00:00:15,921
A Task 1 report has four parts:

6
00:00:15,921 --> 00:00:19,941
an introduction, an overview, and two detail paragraphs.

7
00:00:19,941 --> 00:00:25,182
Please note that every number in this video is made-up illustrative data.

8
00:00:25,182 --> 00:00:29,848
In the exam, you may only describe what is actually in the chart.

9
00:00:31,148 --> 00:00:37,940
The chart shows how many residents visited three cafés between 2010 and 2025.

10
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:41,976
Point two:

11
00:00:41,976 --> 00:00:47,349
the overview states only the general trend, covers all the main features,

12
00:00:47,349 --> 00:00:48,894
and gives no numbers.

13
00:00:48,894 --> 00:00:51,176
Start it with the word Overall.

14
00:00:52,476 --> 00:00:57,420
Overall, Café A grew strongly, whereas Café B declined.

15
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:01,591
Point three:

16
00:01:01,591 --> 00:01:03,261
prepositions with data.

17
00:01:03,261 --> 00:01:07,182
From and to show the starting point and the end point,

18
00:01:07,182 --> 00:01:09,796
while by shows the amount of change.

19
00:01:09,796 --> 00:01:12,264
The numbers here are illustrative.

20
00:01:13,564 --> 00:01:17,282
Café A rose from thirty percent to fifty-five percent,

21
00:01:17,282 --> 00:01:20,380
an increase of twenty-five percentage points.

22
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:24,575
Point four:

23
00:01:24,575 --> 00:01:25,957
relative clauses.

24
00:01:25,957 --> 00:01:33,112
When you add extra information between two commas, use which or who, and don't use that.

25
00:01:34,412 --> 00:01:40,076
Café A, which had the lowest share in 2010, overtook Café B.

26
00:01:43,376 --> 00:01:44,177
Point five:

27
00:01:44,177 --> 00:01:45,124
conditionals.

28
00:01:45,124 --> 00:01:49,858
The second conditional is about unreal situations in the present.

29
00:01:49,858 --> 00:01:54,300
The third conditional is about unreal situations in the past,

30
00:01:54,300 --> 00:02:00,272
and it uses had plus the past participle, and would have plus the past participle.

31
00:02:01,572 --> 00:02:06,732
If the café had stayed open later, it would have attracted more customers.

32
00:02:10,032 --> 00:02:10,857
Point six:

33
00:02:10,857 --> 00:02:11,682
inversion.

34
00:02:11,682 --> 00:02:16,466
After Rarely, Never, or Seldom at the start of a sentence,

35
00:02:16,466 --> 00:02:19,930
put the auxiliary verb before the subject.

36
00:02:19,930 --> 00:02:23,064
Use it only a few times in your essay.

37
00:02:24,364 --> 00:02:27,940
Seldom did the share drop below thirty percent.

38
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:32,482
Common mistakes.

39
00:02:32,482 --> 00:02:34,966
Putting numbers in the overview.

40
00:02:34,966 --> 00:02:38,536
Inventing reasons that the chart doesn't give.

41
00:02:38,536 --> 00:02:44,823
Writing rose to fifty-five from thirty instead of rose from thirty to fifty-five.

42
00:02:44,823 --> 00:02:46,764
Using that after a comma.

43
00:02:46,764 --> 00:02:50,800
And forgetting to invert the auxiliary after Rarely.

44
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:53,358
Quiz one:

45
00:02:53,358 --> 00:02:58,071
the sentence In 2020, Café A reached fifty-five percent.

46
00:02:58,071 --> 00:03:00,595
Is it an overview or a detail?

47
00:03:00,595 --> 00:03:01,353
Quiz two:

48
00:03:01,353 --> 00:03:06,823
fix the mistake in Tourists, that visit the old town, spend more.

49
00:03:06,823 --> 00:03:07,749
Quiz three:

50
00:03:07,749 --> 00:03:11,536
fix the mistake in Rarely visitors come here.

51
00:03:15,836 --> 00:03:16,524
Answers.

52
00:03:16,524 --> 00:03:16,868
One:

53
00:03:16,868 --> 00:03:20,393
detail, because it has a specific number.

54
00:03:20,393 --> 00:03:20,737
Two:

55
00:03:20,737 --> 00:03:27,100
use who instead of that, because there is a comma and it refers to people.

56
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:27,616
Three:

57
00:03:27,616 --> 00:03:30,109
Rarely do visitors come here.

58
00:03:30,109 --> 00:03:33,548
Put the auxiliary do before the subject.

59
00:03:35,848 --> 00:03:36,396
Summary:

60
00:03:36,396 --> 00:03:40,847
paraphrase in the introduction, give an overview with no numbers,

61
00:03:40,847 --> 00:03:44,477
and write two detail paragraphs that match the chart.

62
00:03:44,477 --> 00:03:48,517
Add which clauses, conditionals, and inversion for variety.

63
00:03:48,517 --> 00:03:53,996
Do the week eight exercises in the app, write a Task 1 report in twenty minutes,

64
00:03:53,996 --> 00:03:56,872
and then compare it with the model answer.
